                "question": "What is the difference between preferred stock and common stock?",
                "answer": "Common stock is a residual claim with no cap and no floor: holders get whatever is left, and the dividend is entirely at the board's discretion. Preferred stock fixes two numbers in advance, a liquidation value and a rate applied to it, and pays that rate and nothing more. Preferred ranks ahead of common in a wind-up and behind every creditor, and it normally carries no vote."
